  "details": "Pre-Caching:\n- When searching through worlds in-game, or on the website, having the option to have a world pre-downloaded and ready to play would help make world hopping go a lot smoother.  \nAuto-Cache:\n- Sometimes worlds update and they need to be pre-cached again. Auto-caching can be enabled via a check mark under \"cache options\" for that world, and that world will be mark to always be up to date. (Updates upon logging in. Auto-cache list is local to the device.)\nCached Worlds List:\n- A list of worlds read from your local cache. This serves as a means for navigating through worlds you have in cache, either from playing the world, or pre-caching it. (It should ignore levels that have been updated or denote they have been updated.)\n\nOther stuff:\n- Pre-caching/Auto-caching of course would have to happen while logged in (unless an external cache manager can be made, which would be a whole idea on its own). Perhaps it can happen in the background after you finish downloading any worlds or avatars.\n\n- Pre-caching settings, such as pausing all or specific pre-caching operations (Pre-cache, auto-cache, etc), and pre-cache download speed could be added.",
